WEBVTT

1
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.541
<b>In the previous verse, Krishna said to Arjuna,</b>

2
00:01:04.541 --> 00:01:05.708
<b>"Arjuna,</b>

3
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:08.958
<b>in the past, there were many sage-like beings</b>

4
00:01:08.958 --> 00:01:15.541
<b>who performed their duties without desire</b>
<b>for rewards and attained liberation.</b>

5
00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:20.583
<b>You too should follow their </b>
<b>path and perform your duties."</b>

6
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.666
<b>Karma,</b>

7
00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:26.791
<b>this word appears countless times </b>
<b>in the Vedas and scriptures,</b>

8
00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:30.833
<b>and many become confused by its meaning.</b>

9
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:32.833
<b>Arjuna too was confused,</b>

10
00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:40.375
<b>which is why he was ready to abandon the battle </b>
<b>and his worldly duties to retreat to the forest.</b>

11
00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:41.083
<b>Now</b>

12
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:46.541
<b>in the fourth chapter, in these sixteenth, </b>
<b>seventeenth, and eighteenth verses,</b>

13
00:01:46.541 --> 00:01:47.916
<b>Krishna</b>

14
00:01:47.916 --> 00:01:53.250
<b>is giving a very detailed explanation </b>
<b>of the word Karma.</b>

15
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.208
<b>First, in the sixteenth verse, Krishna says,</b>

16
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:04.333
<b>"Arjun,</b>

17
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:08.791
<b>Even the wise become confused in understanding</b>

18
00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:12.375
<b>what is action and what is inaction.</b>

19
00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:16.958
<b>I shall now give you complete </b>
<b>knowledge about action,</b>

20
00:02:16.958 --> 00:02:21.000
<b>knowing which you shall be </b>
<b>freed from all miseries."</b>

21
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.041
<b>Krishna acknowledges here</b>

22
00:02:23.041 --> 00:02:29.541
<b>that Karma is a subject that proves complex</b>
<b>even for many wise ones.</b>

23
00:02:29.541 --> 00:02:32.083
<b>The same happened with Arjuna –</b>

24
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:38.541
<b>he had even suggested abandoning the </b>
<b>battle to live as a mendicant in the forest.</b>

25
00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:43.833
<b>He thought by avoiding the action of war, </b>
<b>he would be free from sin.</b>

26
00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:45.291
<b>But this isn't so.</b>

27
00:02:45.291 --> 00:02:47.208
<b>Even if action is not performed,</b>

28
00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:50.500
<b>you are not freed from the bonds of action.</b>

29
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.166
<b>This matter is quite deep,</b>

30
00:02:52.166 --> 00:02:55.666
<b>which is why Krishna explains it in the next verse.</b>

31
00:02:55.666 --> 00:03:01.250
<b>In the seventeenth verse, Krishna explains </b>
<b>that action, forbidden action, and inaction –</b>

32
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.750
<b>these three are different forms of action,</b>

33
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:08.500
<b>and though their differences are </b>
<b>difficult to understand, it is essential to do so.</b>

34
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.666
<b>Krishna says this because</b>

35
00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:16.375
<b>those who seek liberation must necessarily</b>
<b>understand the distinction between these three.</b>

36
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:19.250
<b>Let us understand these differences.</b>

37
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.083
<b>Action (Karma) –</b>

38
00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:26.291
<b>Acts performed according to Vedic principles </b>
<b>that bring good material results.</b>

39
00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:27.916
<b>Here there is action,</b>

40
00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:29.875
<b>it follows Vedic principles,</b>

41
00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.416
<b>and there is desire for the fruit of action.</b>

42
00:03:32.416 --> 00:03:35.791
<b>Such action that is not done </b>
<b>with the intention to harm,</b>

43
00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:40.208
<b>but solely for personal benefit.</b>

44
00:03:40.208 --> 00:03:41.500
<b>Forbidden action (Vikarma) -</b>

45
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:45.541
<b>This is exactly opposite to the above definition.</b>

46
00:03:45.541 --> 00:03:50.291
<b>These are acts performed </b>
<b>against Vedic principles,</b>

47
00:03:50.291 --> 00:03:54.333
<b>such as with the intention to </b>
<b>cause unjust harm to others.</b>

48
00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.291
<b>Certainly,</b>

49
00:03:55.291 --> 00:03:59.875
<b>the results of forbidden actions are negative.</b>

50
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:01.291
<b>And the third is</b>

51
00:04:01.291 --> 00:04:02.291
<b>Inaction (Akarma) –</b>

52
00:04:02.291 --> 00:04:09.625
<b>meaning acts performed solely in surrender </b>
<b>to Lord Krishna, only for His pleasure.</b>

53
00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:13.166
<b>And inaction has no material </b>
<b>results attached to it –</b>

54
00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:14.791
<b>neither positive</b>

55
00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:17.000
<b>nor negative.</b>

56
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.958
<b>Understand this through this example – </b>

57
00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:23.333
<b>someone in the family cooks for others.</b>

58
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:28.000
<b>If it was done for others' appreciation, it is action.</b>

59
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.375
<b>If it was done solely and exclusively as a duty </b>
<b>received from God,</b>

60
00:04:32.375 --> 00:04:36.666
<b>for His pleasure, it becomes inaction.</b>

61
00:04:36.666 --> 00:04:42.125
<b>But if knowingly, something is added to the </b>
<b>food that would harm someone's health,</b>

62
00:04:42.125 --> 00:04:51.625
<b>or if tasty food is served to later deceive </b>
<b>that person into some fraud –</b>

63
00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:55.708
<b>then this is certainly forbidden action.</b>

64
00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:56.333
<b>Now</b>

65
00:04:56.333 --> 00:05:01.333
<b>continuing this topic in the </b>
<b>eighteenth verse, Krishna says –</b>

66
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:07.166
<b>a wise person is one who sees inaction in action, </b>
<b>and action in inaction.</b>

67
00:05:07.166 --> 00:05:14.416
<b>And one who understands this while engaging in </b>
<b>worldly activities remains unaffected by results.</b>

68
00:05:14.416 --> 00:05:17.291
<b>Let us understand this.</b>

69
00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:22.541
<b>Action in inaction - meaning action that</b>
<b>is not performed for personal gain,</b>

70
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:28.916
<b>but solely and exclusively in surrender </b>
<b>to Krishna, to please Him.</b>

71
00:05:28.916 --> 00:05:30.125
<b>For example –</b>

72
00:05:30.125 --> 00:05:36.708
<b>the duties you perform, you sincerely believe</b>
<b>that this is Krishna's given duty,</b>

73
00:05:36.708 --> 00:05:42.166
<b>this is devotion to Him, and performing </b>
<b>this action will please Him.</b>

74
00:05:42.166 --> 00:05:44.666
<b>Now understand inaction in action –</b>

75
00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:49.041
<b>this is important because this</b>
<b>was Arjuna's dilemma too,</b>

76
00:05:49.041 --> 00:05:55.791
<b>which made him talk about renouncing </b>
<b>everything and going to the forest.</b>

77
00:05:55.791 --> 00:05:57.750
<b>Inaction in action -</b>

78
00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:02.375
<b>meaning that which appears </b>
<b>like inaction, but isn't.</b>

79
00:06:02.375 --> 00:06:03.750
<b>For example,</b>

80
00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:08.333
<b>if someone takes incomplete knowledge </b>
<b>and becomes a sage, takes sannyasa,</b>

81
00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:11.708
<b>it will appear that they are </b>
<b>not performing any action,</b>

82
00:06:11.708 --> 00:06:18.458
<b>but if their mind is still attached</b>
<b>to desires, still craves for sweets,</b>

83
00:06:18.458 --> 00:06:20.750
<b>is troubled by bodily desires,</b>

84
00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.750
<b>then this may not be physical action </b>
<b>but is certainly mental action.</b>

85
00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:29.000
<b>If Arjuna too had gone to the</b>
<b>forest without being purified,</b>

86
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:34.083
<b>he would have remained inactive but </b>
<b>mentally disturbed and impure.</b>

87
00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:37.625
<b>This too would have been action in inaction.</b>

88
00:06:37.625 --> 00:06:42.666
<b>Action is not just physical activity, </b>
<b>it is mental activity too.</b>

89
00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:44.000
<b>For this reason,</b>

90
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.208
<b>purity of mind is paramount.</b>

91
00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:03.000
<b>The essence of understanding karma, </b>
<b>negative karma, and non-karma</b>

92
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:09.375
<b>lies in your intention behind the action,</b>

93
00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:15.708
<b>and whether that action aligns with</b>
<b>spiritual principles or not.</b>

94
00:07:15.708 --> 00:07:25.208
<b>Any action performed within righteous </b>
<b>boundaries, without seeking personal gain,</b>

95
00:07:25.208 --> 00:07:27.333
<b>becomes non-karma.</b>

96
00:07:27.333 --> 00:07:32.333
<b>It creates no bonds of merit or sin.</b>

97
00:07:32.333 --> 00:07:37.291
<b>When you perform activities </b>
<b>at home, work, or in society</b>

98
00:07:37.291 --> 00:07:44.916
<b>free from personal motives, solely to serve others,</b>

99
00:07:44.916 --> 00:07:51.166
<b>and also view them as divine responsibilities –</b>

100
00:07:51.166 --> 00:07:56.333
<b>these activities transform into non-karma.</b>

101
00:07:56.333 --> 00:07:58.083
<b>For instance,</b>

102
00:07:58.083 --> 00:08:03.000
<b>when you help a colleague purely for their benefit,</b>

103
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:08.875
<b>expecting nothing in return –</b>

104
00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:12.250
<b>this becomes a type of non-karma.</b>

105
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:17.208
<b>You can call this karma within non-karma.</b>

106
00:08:17.208 --> 00:08:21.208
<b>Even amidst countless busy activities,</b>

107
00:08:21.208 --> 00:08:31.041
<b>if you detach from their outcomes </b>
<b>and perform them as service to the divine,</b>

108
00:08:31.041 --> 00:08:34.333
<b>you're practicing non-karma.</b>

109
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:41.125
<b>This doesn't mean you're careless about results;</b>

110
00:08:41.125 --> 00:08:50.541
<b>rather, your inner peace and contentment </b>
<b>don't depend on outcomes.</b>

111
00:08:50.541 --> 00:08:56.041
<b>Whether results are good or bad, </b>
<b>you remain unaffected –</b>

112
00:08:56.041 --> 00:08:58.333
<b>neither excited nor disturbed.</b>

113
00:08:58.333 --> 00:09:03.333
<b>You simply move on to your next duty.</b>

114
00:09:03.333 --> 00:09:09.541
<b>Your focus remains solely on duty,</b>

115
00:09:09.541 --> 00:09:11.166
<b>not on outcomes.</b>

116
00:09:11.166 --> 00:09:12.458
<b>Whereas,</b>

117
00:09:12.458 --> 00:09:15.708
<b>conversely, understand this well –</b>

118
00:09:15.708 --> 00:09:18.875
<b>inaction is not non-karma.</b>

119
00:09:18.875 --> 00:09:25.083
<b>If you avoid responsibilities out of fear or pressure,</b>

120
00:09:25.083 --> 00:09:28.375
<b>this can never be non-karma.</b>

121
00:09:28.375 --> 00:09:29.208
<b>and</b>

122
00:09:29.208 --> 00:09:37.791
<b>escaping duty keeps you bound in </b>
<b>the cycle of merit and sin.</b>

123
00:09:37.791 --> 00:09:43.458
<b>Understand and recognize this distinction.</b>

124
00:09:47.916 --> 00:09:55.833
<b>In family life, understanding and practicing</b>
<b>karma and non-karma is entirely possible.</b>

125
00:09:55.833 --> 00:10:00.791
<b>Fulfilling family duties is crucial –</b>

126
00:10:00.791 --> 00:10:06.333
<b>whether it's children's education,</b>
<b>helping with household tasks,</b>

127
00:10:06.333 --> 00:10:10.791
<b>or caring for elderly family members.</b>

128
00:10:10.791 --> 00:10:16.833
<b>When you perform these duties with </b>
<b>complete devotion and love,</b>

129
00:10:16.833 --> 00:10:25.916
<b>expecting no appreciation, help, </b>
<b>or personal gain in return –</b>

130
00:10:25.916 --> 00:10:30.291
<b>this exemplifies karma within non-karma.</b>

131
00:10:30.291 --> 00:10:35.291
<b>This doesn't mean you're indifferent to results.</b>

132
00:10:35.291 --> 00:10:36.958
<b>For instance,</b>

133
00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:40.208
<b>if your child scores poorly,</b>

134
00:10:40.208 --> 00:10:44.083
<b>it doesn't mean you're unconcerned.</b>

135
00:10:44.083 --> 00:10:44.875
<b>But</b>

136
00:10:44.875 --> 00:10:49.000
<b>understand the difference between </b>
<b>concern and worry.</b>

137
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.375
<b>Worrying and grieving are futile.</b>

138
00:10:52.375 --> 00:10:53.500
<b>Ultimately,</b>

139
00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.791
<b>if grades aren't good,</b>

140
00:10:55.791 --> 00:11:02.250
<b>it's simply life's circumstance where you </b>
<b>must perform your duty again,</b>

141
00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:05.166
<b>help your child again,</b>

142
00:11:05.166 --> 00:11:09.333
<b>make every possible effort again.</b>

143
00:11:09.333 --> 00:11:12.208
<b>This isn't negligence.</b>

144
00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:16.708
<b>Detachment from results simply means</b>

145
00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:21.333
<b>good outcomes don't overly excite you,</b>

146
00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:24.583
<b>and bad outcomes don't sadden you.</b>

147
00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.458
<b>Conversely,</b>

148
00:11:26.458 --> 00:11:34.875
<b>if you ignore your responsibilities </b>
<b>to avoid trouble, remaining passive,</b>

149
00:11:34.875 --> 00:11:39.208
<b>this becomes karma within non-karma.</b>

150
00:11:39.208 --> 00:11:45.041
<b>Escaping duty to avoid pain is a choice, a karma.</b>

151
00:11:45.041 --> 00:11:50.041
<b>It will have consequences, and you'll face them.</b>

152
00:11:50.041 --> 00:11:51.541
<b>For example,</b>

153
00:11:51.541 --> 00:11:56.541
<b>if you neglect caring for an elderly family member</b>

154
00:11:56.541 --> 00:12:01.750
<b>simply because it's too demanding –</b>

155
00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:10.250
<b>such inaction becomes karma, </b>
<b>and that too negative karma.</b>

156
00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.666
<b>Understand this distinction</b>

157
00:12:12.666 --> 00:12:15.416
<b>and strive for 'non-karma'.</b>

158
00:12:19.583 --> 00:12:24.625
<b>Understanding karma within non-karma </b>
<b>and non-karma within karma</b>

159
00:12:24.625 --> 00:12:30.125
<b>can profoundly impact your professional life.</b>

160
00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:34.458
<b>In a professional setting, karma </b>
<b>within non-karma means</b>

161
00:12:34.458 --> 00:12:40.250
<b>fulfilling responsibilities with complete </b>
<b>dedication and surrender,</b>

162
00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:44.458
<b>while remaining detached from outcomes.</b>

163
00:12:44.458 --> 00:12:49.875
<b>Suppose you lead a project with full commitment,</b>

164
00:12:49.875 --> 00:12:53.583
<b>sparing no effort,</b>

165
00:12:53.583 --> 00:13:00.416
<b>yet knowing results aren't in your control. </b>

166
00:13:00.416 --> 00:13:06.458
<b>Whether outcomes are good or bad, </b>
<b>you accept them gracefully.</b>

167
00:13:06.458 --> 00:13:14.583
<b>Without excitement or distress, you move </b>
<b>on to your next responsibility.</b>

168
00:13:14.583 --> 00:13:19.916
<b>This perspective exemplifies </b>
<b>karma within non-karma,</b>

169
00:13:19.916 --> 00:13:25.083
<b>where your focus remains on your duty.</b>

170
00:13:25.083 --> 00:13:31.125
<b>This helps maintain mental peace and balance.</b>

171
00:13:31.125 --> 00:13:33.041
<b>For instance,</b>

172
00:13:33.041 --> 00:13:37.000
<b>if an organization faces financial crisis,</b>

173
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.500
<b>employee layoffs might become necessary –</b>

174
00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:47.291
<b>seemingly harsh and negative.</b>

175
00:13:47.291 --> 00:13:48.458
<b>But</b>

176
00:13:48.458 --> 00:13:54.833
<b>if you choose this option after </b>
<b>exploring all alternatives,</b>

177
00:13:54.833 --> 00:14:04.000
<b>if you perform this task with compassion, duty</b>
<b>-bound, and detached from personal emotions – </b>

178
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:11.875
<b>even such a challenging task becomes like</b>
<b>karma within non-karma.</b>

179
00:14:11.875 --> 00:14:15.750
<b>Conversely, non-karma within karma occurs</b>

180
00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:24.041
<b>when someone ignores necessary actions, </b>
<b>evades responsibility out of fear</b>

181
00:14:24.041 --> 00:14:26.333
<b>or to avoid adverse outcomes.</b>

182
00:14:26.333 --> 00:14:28.208
<b>For example,</b>

183
00:14:28.208 --> 00:14:33.708
<b>when a senior officer witnesses unethical</b>
<b>practices in the organization</b>

184
00:14:33.708 --> 00:14:34.666
<b>but</b>

185
00:14:34.666 --> 00:14:43.333
<b>remains silent due to self-interest or to</b>
<b>avoid conflict – simply turning a blind eye –</b>

186
00:14:43.333 --> 00:14:47.500
<b>this becomes karma of choosing inaction.</b>

187
00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.416
<b>This is karma within non-karma.</b>

188
00:14:50.416 --> 00:14:53.958
<b>Such inaction will have negative consequences.</b>

189
00:14:53.958 --> 00:15:01.541
<b>Understanding and implementing this </b>
<b>distinction in professional settings is crucial.</b>

